  skos:scopeNote "Publications of geology, such as books, periodicals, magazines, etc."@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_GL_geopark
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader ddetc:GI_GL_geologicalLiterature ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.36.2 Geopark"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Study and management of the UNESCO Geopark that are single, unified geographical areas where sites and landscapes of international geological significance are managed with a holistic concept of protection, education and sustainable development."@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_GM_digitalGeologicalMapping
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader ddetc:GI_GM_geologicMapping ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.9.3 Digital geological mapping"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Study or documentation of the process of using computer software to create a digital geological map or to construct database of geological maps."@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_GM_geologicMapping
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/metadata-codelist/TopicCategory/geoscientificInformation> ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:narrower ddetc:GI_GM_digitalGeologicalMapping ;
  skos:narrower ddetc:GI_GM_geologicalCompilation ;
  skos:narrower ddetc:GI_GM_geologicalSurvey ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.9 Geologic mapping"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Study or documentation of the interpretive, geoscientific processes to produce depictions of the distribution of rocks and geologic structures in the Earth. Scope includes a range of map products for many different uses, including assessing ground-water quality and contamination risks; predicting earthquake, volcano, and landslide hazards; characterizing energy and mineral resources and their extraction costs; waste repository siting; land management and land-use planning; and general education. The products include geological, tectonic, seismological, geophysical and geochemical maps at different scales."@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_GM_geologicalCompilation
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader ddetc:GI_GM_geologicMapping ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.9.2 Geological compilation"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Study or documentation of geoscience map compilation. A geological map may be compiled from other maps, usually of larger scale, or may be produced from original geoscientific surveys and photogrammetric compilations."@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_GM_geologicalSurvey
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader ddetc:GI_GM_geologicMapping ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.9.1 Geological survey"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Study or documentation of the process of collecting geological data by a variety of methods such as field profiling, drilling, remote sensing and sampling etc."@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_GPH_appliedGeomorphology
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader ddetc:GI_GPH_geomorphology ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.28.4 Applied geomorphology"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Study of the use of principles and methods of geomorphology to solve practical problems. It links the study of geomorphology closely to the transformation of nature and human decision-making processes. It relates to environmental studies, resource surveys, disaster prevention, soil and water conservation, etc. Applied geomorphology includes multiple sub-fields, for example, agricultural geomorphology, engineering geomorphology and mining geomorphology."@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_GPH_climaticGeomorphology
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader ddetc:GI_GPH_geomorphology ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.28.7 Climatic geomorphology"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Study of the processes of landform formation and their evolution under different climatic conditions. "@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_GPH_dynamicalGeomorphology
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader ddetc:GI_GPH_geomorphology ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.28.2 Dynamical geomorphology"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Study of the mechanisms of landform evolution focused on geomorphic processes. It can be divided into endodynamic geomorphology and exokinetic geomorphology. It applies the principles and methods of basic sciences such as mathematics, physics and chemistry, focusing on the modern process of landform formation and the relationship between landform and various action variables."@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_GPH_experimentalGeomorphology
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader ddetc:GI_GPH_geomorphology ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.28.5 Experimental geomorphology"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "The study of geomorphic process through indoor scale modelling or observation of a selected geomorphic feature under controlled conditions to reveal relationships between the development of landforms and different factors. "@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_GPH_fractalGeomorphology
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader ddetc:GI_GPH_geomorphology ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.28.9 Fractal geomorphology"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Study of the use of fractal methods and principles to study the surface morphology and its occurrence, development and distribution."@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_GPH_geomorphologicalMapping
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader ddetc:GI_GPH_geomorphology ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.28.6 Geomorphological mapping"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Description of the process of visualizing the scale, spatial distribution, classification or regionalization of various geomorphological objects and phenomena on a map. It is an important method and tool for geomorphological investigation and research, as well as a powerful illustration and supplement to the written description of geomorphological phenomena. The results of geomorphological mapping include geomorphological classification maps, geomorphological regionalization maps, etc."@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_GPH_geomorphology
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/metadata-codelist/TopicCategory/geoscientificInformation> ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:narrower ddetc:GI_GPH_appliedGeomorphology ;
  skos:narrower ddetc:GI_GPH_climaticGeomorphology ;
  skos:narrower ddetc:GI_GPH_dynamicalGeomorphology ;
  skos:narrower ddetc:GI_GPH_experimentalGeomorphology ;
  skos:narrower ddetc:GI_GPH_fractalGeomorphology ;
  skos:narrower ddetc:GI_GPH_geomorphologicalMapping ;
  skos:narrower ddetc:GI_GPH_historicalGeomorphology ;
  skos:narrower ddetc:GI_GPH_quantitativeGeomorphology ;
  skos:narrower ddetc:GI_GPH_regionalGeomorphology ;
  skos:narrower ddetc:GI_GPH_specialGeomorphology ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.28 Geomorphology"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Study of the origin and evolution of physiography, topographic and bathymetric features created by physical, chemical or biological processes operating at or near the Earth's surface."@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_GPH_historicalGeomorphology
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader ddetc:GI_GPH_geomorphology ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.28.10 Historical geomorphology"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Study of the temporal sequence of development of geomorphic features."@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_GPH_quantitativeGeomorphology
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader ddetc:GI_GPH_geomorphology ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.28.8 Quantitative geomorphology"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Study of land surface morphology, its formation and development through the analysis of quantitative data using mathematical methods. It includes the acquisition of quantitative data, the quantification of non-quantitative information, the processing and analysis of data, the creation of models and the simulation of geomorphological processes.Includes digital geomorphology, which is a branch of geomorphology that studies surface morphology, landform types, spatial distribution, geomorphic formation and evolution process through comprehensive analysis of remote sensing images, digital terrain model (DTM) and other relevant geomorphic data in a geographic information system environment."@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_GPH_regionalGeomorphology
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader ddetc:GI_GPH_geomorphology ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.28.3 Regional geomorphology"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Study of the geomorphology of an area, with analysis of topographic characteristics, genetic dynamics, geomorphic evolution, geographical distribution and composition characteristics. Includes studies at different spatial scales, such as global geomorphology, intercontinental geomorphology, plate geomorphology, national geomorphology, and local regional geomorphology etc."@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_GPH_specialGeomorphology
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader ddetc:GI_GPH_geomorphology ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.28.1 Special geomorphology"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Study of the landforms and their geomorphic evolution formed by some geological agents (such as fluvial landforms, aeolian landform, glacial landform, karst landform, coastal landform, etc.) as its independent research object."@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_GTH_appliedGeothermics
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader ddetc:GI_GTH_geothermics ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.32.2 Applied geothermics"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Studies that investigate geothermal resource types, origin and distribution, geothermal resource exploration, geothermal resource evaluation, geothermal resource development and utilization, and geothermal disaster."@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_GTH_dryHotRock
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader ddetc:GI_GTH_geothermics ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.32.4 Dry hot rock"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Study of underground dry hot rock exploration and utility, etc."@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_GTH_geothermalEnergy
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader ddetc:GI_GTH_geothermics ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.32.3 Geothermal energy"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Study of heat energy that comes from the subsurface of the earth which contained in the rocks and fluids beneath the crust and originates from the formation of the planet or geological movements and radioactive decay of mass materials."@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_GTH_geothermics
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/metadata-codelist/TopicCategory/geoscientificInformation> ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:narrower ddetc:GI_GTH_appliedGeothermics ;
  skos:narrower ddetc:GI_GTH_dryHotRock ;
  skos:narrower ddetc:GI_GTH_geothermalEnergy ;
  skos:narrower ddetc:GI_GTH_theoreticalGeothermics ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.32 Geothermics"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Study of heat from within the Earth as a natural resource. It includes geothermal geology, geothermal exploration, geothermal exploitation, geothermal tourism, etc."@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_GTH_theoreticalGeothermics
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader ddetc:GI_GTH_geothermics ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.32.1 Theoretical geothermics"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Study of fundamental topics related to heat in the Earth such as the thermal structure of crust and mantle, the deep thermal state and the formation mechanism and control factors of the thermal evolution of lithosphere structure."@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_HG_geologicalProcessesOfGroundwater
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader ddetc:GI_HG_hydrogeology ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.10.4 Geological processes of groundwater"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Study of the relationship between geologic processes and the occurrence and movement of groundwater."@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_HG_groundwaterDependentEcosystems
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader ddetc:GI_HG_hydrogeology ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.10.5 Groundwater dependent ecosystems"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Study of ecosystems that depend on groundwater permanently or intermittently to meet all or some of their water requirements so as to maintain their communities of plants and animals, ecological processes and ecosystem services."@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_HG_groundwaterFlow
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader ddetc:GI_HG_hydrogeology ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.10.2 Groundwater flow"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Study of he movement of water through soil or rock bodies in the subsurface."@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_HG_groundwaterQuality
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader ddetc:GI_HG_hydrogeology ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.10.3 Groundwater quality"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Study of the physical, chemical and biological properties of groundwater related to its utilization for human activities."@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_HG_hydrogeology
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/metadata-codelist/TopicCategory/geoscientificInformation> ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:narrower ddetc:GI_HG_geologicalProcessesOfGroundwater ;
  skos:narrower ddetc:GI_HG_groundwaterDependentEcosystems ;
  skos:narrower ddetc:GI_HG_groundwaterFlow ;
  skos:narrower ddetc:GI_HG_groundwaterQuality ;
  skos:narrower ddetc:GI_HG_storageOfGroundwater ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.10 Hydrogeology"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Study of the distribution and movement of groundwater in the soil and rocks of the Earth's crust, commonly in aquifers. Geology of ground water and hydrology, also including ground water dynamic, mining hydrogeology, regional hydrogeology, etc."@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_HG_storageOfGroundwater
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader ddetc:GI_HG_hydrogeology ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.10.1 Storage of groundwater"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Study of the hydrological properties of rock and soil as they relate to water as a constituent of the rock body."@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_MAP_MagmaticPetrology
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/metadata-codelist/TopicCategory/geoscientificInformation> ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:narrower ddetc:GI_MAP_compositionAndClassification ;
  skos:narrower ddetc:GI_MAP_geochemicalProperties ;
  skos:narrower ddetc:GI_MAP_magmatismAndOrigin ;
  skos:narrower ddetc:GI_MAP_physicalProperties ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.5Magmatic petrology"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Study of macroscopic and microscopic mineralogical and chemical composition of igneous rocks (or magmatic rocks)—formed through the cooling and solidification of molten material (magma or lava) either within the earth’s crust or at crust the surface of the earth.The modern study of igneous rocks utilizes many techniques, some of them developed in the fields of chemistry, physics, or other earth sciences. Mineralogy, crystallography, and isotopy studies are common methods used in igneous petrology.(from “Igneous rocks” by Jerram D. and Petford N. (2004), Robin Gill (2010) and Wikipedia)."@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_MAP_compositionAndClassification
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader ddetc:GI_MAP_MagmaticPetrology ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.5.1 Composition and classification"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Mineral and geochemical composition of igneous rocks. The classification of igneous rocks refers to classifying igneous rocks according to their mineral and geochemical compositions. The rocks are generally classified into ultramafic, mafic, intermediate, and acidic igneous rocks, and some special and unclassified igneous rocks.(from “Igneous rocks” by Tomkeieff S.T.(1983), R.W.Le Maitre (2002), Best M G (2003) and Wikipedia)"@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_MAP_geochemicalProperties
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader ddetc:GI_MAP_MagmaticPetrology ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.5.2 Geochemical properties"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Study of major, trace element, and isotopic composition of igneous rocks. The chemistry of igneous systems provides clues to many important whole-earth evolution processes, including the origins of igneous, processes and timing of planetary differentiation, the production and destruction of the lithosphere, and the relationships between magmatic styles, composition, crust growth, mantle-crust convection, and plate-tectonic environment."@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_MAP_magmatismAndOrigin
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader ddetc:GI_MAP_MagmaticPetrology ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.5.4 Magmatism and origin"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Study ofthe origin and emplacement of magma within or at the surface of the outer layers of a terrestrial planet to form igneous rocks. Includes the production, intrusion, and extrusion of magma or lava. Volcanism is the surface expression of magmatism.The origin of igneous rocks is to study the source of magma, magma generation, magmatism, and other properties related to igneous formation.(from “Igneous rocks” by Robin Gill (2010) and Wikipedia)"@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_MAP_physicalProperties
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader ddetc:GI_MAP_MagmaticPetrology ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.5.3 Physical properties"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Study of the observable, measurable, and describable physical properties of igneous rocks and magma processes, including the occurrence in the field, texture, (ductile and brittle) structure of igneous rocks, as well as the physical properties of magma, such as temperature, pressure, and rheology etc.(from “Igneous rocks” by Jerram D. and Petford N. (2004) and Wikipedia)"@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_MG_coastalMorphoDynamics
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader ddetc:GI_MG_marineGeology ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.15.10Coastal morphodynamics"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Study of the changes in the morphology of the coastal zone, including the topography of the sea bed and the shoreline planform, in connection with waves, currents, tides and sea level rise."@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_MG_marineGeochemistry
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader ddetc:GI_MG_marineGeology ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.15.7 Marine geochemistry"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Study of the chemistry of geological materials such as rocks, sediments and water from the ocean or ocean floor."@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_MG_marineGeochronology
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader ddetc:GI_MG_marineGeology ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.15.5 Marine geochronology"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Determination of ages and time intervals for geologic materials, including marine sediments, and processes on geologic, archeologic, and historic time scales. It is the science of investigating the chronology of the earth constituents as induced from geologic data, based on absolute and relative dating methods."@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_MG_marineGeohazards
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader ddetc:GI_MG_marineGeology ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.15.9Marine geohazards"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Study of geological conditions at the sea floor or within sub-bottom sediments that could result in dangerous or catastrophic events with attendant risks to life and/or infrastructure. The major marine geohazards are coastal erosion, seawater intrusion, earthquakes, submarine landslides, subsidence, tsunamis, natural gas hydrate dissociation, seabed sand waves, shallow gas, overpressure strata, gas chimneys, mud volcanoes and mud diapirism"@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_MG_marineGeology
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/metadata-codelist/TopicCategory/geoscientificInformation> ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:narrower ddetc:GI_MG_coastalMorphoDynamics ;
  skos:narrower ddetc:GI_MG_marineGeochemistry ;
  skos:narrower ddetc:GI_MG_marineGeochronology ;
  skos:narrower ddetc:GI_MG_marineGeohazards ;
  skos:narrower ddetc:GI_MG_marinePaleontologyAndMicropaleontology ;
  skos:narrower ddetc:GI_MG_marinePetrology ;
  skos:narrower ddetc:GI_MG_marineSedimentDynamics ;
  skos:narrower ddetc:GI_MG_marineSedimentology ;
  skos:narrower ddetc:GI_MG_paleoceanographyAndPaleoclimatology ;
  skos:narrower ddetc:GI_MG_seafloorHabitat ;
  skos:narrower ddetc:GI_MG_seafloorTectonicsAndGeodynamics ;
  skos:narrower ddetc:GI_MG_submarineGeomorphology ;
  skos:narrower ddetc:GI_MG_subseafloorBiosphere ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.15 Marine geology"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Study of the history and structure of the ocean floor from shorelines to the continental shelf and deep sea. It involves geophysical, geochemical, sedimentological and paleontological investigations of the ocean floor and coastal zone."@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_MG_marinePaleontologyAndMicropaleontology
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader ddetc:GI_MG_marineGeology ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.15.11Marine paleontology and micropaleontology"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Study of ancient fossils and microfossils in the sediments in order to reconstruct past conditions of oceans and environments."@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_MG_marinePetrology
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader ddetc:GI_MG_marineGeology ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.15.6 Marine petrology"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Study of the mineralogy, textures, and chemical composition of igneous, sedimentary, and metamorphic rocks from the ocean floor, since their composition reflects the conditions at which they were formed and the time they needed to develop."@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_MG_marineSedimentDynamics
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader ddetc:GI_MG_marineGeology ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.15.3 Marine sediment dynamics"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Study of the motion of sediment particles during their formation, transport, and settling processes (Zhang, 2014)."@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_MG_marineSedimentology
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader ddetc:GI_MG_marineGeology ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.15.2 Marine sedimentology"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Description, classification, modeling, and interpretation of marine sediments so as to determine the physical, chemical, and biological processes by which they formed."@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_MG_paleoceanographyAndPaleoclimatology
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader ddetc:GI_MG_marineGeology ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.15.4 Paleoceanography and paleoclimatology"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Study of the circulation, chemistry, biology, geology and patterns of sedimentation and biological productivity of the oceansand climates as they were in the past, from a few hundred years to billions of years ago (Thomas, 2009)."@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_MG_seafloorHabitat
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader ddetc:GI_MG_marineGeology ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.15.12 Seafloor habitat"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Study of physical structure, dimensions, and biological characteristics of specific species or groups of species occupying the seafloor (Diaz et al. 2004)."@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_MG_seafloorTectonicsAndGeodynamics
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader ddetc:GI_MG_marineGeology ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.15.8 Seafloor tectonics and geodynamics"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Study of the genesis, aging, motion, and destruction of oceanic plates (Koppers and Coggon, 2020) and their interactions with the earth’s interior."@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_MG_submarineGeomorphology
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader ddetc:GI_MG_marineGeology ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.15.1 Submarine geomorphology"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Study of the morphology and evolution of seafloor landforms, and the processes responsible for their formation, in particular erosion and depositional processes, sediment movement and deformation, volcanic activity, fluid migration, and anthropogenic impacts."@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_MG_subseafloorBiosphere
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader ddetc:GI_MG_marineGeology ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.15.13 Subseafloor biosphere"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Study of the subseafloor ecosystem and environments (e.g., hydrothermal systems and cold seeps) that sustain them."@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_MI_chemicalCompositionAndCrystalStructure
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader ddetc:GI_MI_mineralogy ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.16.5 Chemical composition and crystal structure"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Study of the identity and number of the chemical elements that make up any particular mineralthe ordered arrangement of atoms, ions or molecules in a crystalline material."@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_MI_crystallography
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader ddetc:GI_MI_mineralogy ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.16.2 Crystallography"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Study of the external form and the crystal structure of crystalline solids and the principles that govern their growth, shape, and internal atomic arrangement."@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_MI_mineralClassificationAndDescription
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader ddetc:GI_MI_mineralogy ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.16.4 Mineral classification and description"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Study ofschemes for mineral classifications that are determined in the light of chemical composition and internal structure."@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_MI_mineralGenesisAndItsOccurrence
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader ddetc:GI_MI_mineralogy ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.16.3 Mineral genesis and occurrence"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Study of minerals characteristics, species and assemblages as they relate to the physical and chemical conditions ofconditions and genetic processes."@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_MI_mineralPropertiesAndItsApplications
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
  rdf:type skos:Concept ;
  skos:broader ddetc:GI_MI_mineralogy ;
  skos:inScheme <https://www.ddeworld.org/resource/codelist/topicCategory> ;
  skos:prefLabel "8.16.1 Mineral properties and applications"@en ;
  skos:scopeNote "Study of the properties of minerals, for understanding geological phenomena and synthesizing new materials."@en ;
.
ddetc:GI_MI_mineralogy
  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ;
